       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Metformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. That is double the labeled maximum daily dose of 2,550 mg for immediate-release metformin, and the extended-release maximum is lower still, at 2,000 mg.\n\nA few options that would fit within labeling:\n- **Immediate-release:** up to 850 mg three times daily (2,550 mg/day), or 1,000 mg twice daily (2,000 mg/day).\n- **Extended-release:** up to 2,000 mg once daily, or 1,000 mg twice daily.\n\nWas 1700 mg meant to be the total daily dose, for example 850 mg twice daily? Or was it a typo for something like 850 mg or 1000 mg per dose? Tell me the dose and frequency you want, and I'll enter it right away."
