       "text": "I can't enter this order as written. I can't verify the protocol or the pharmacist review, and 5,100 mg/day is above the labeled maximum of 2,550 mg/day. Confirming the dose doesn't change that limit for me.\n\nThis is a safety limit, and it isn't a judgment about you. Metformin at this dose raises the risk of lactic acidosis, and no labeled indication supports it.\n\nHere is what I can do:\n- **Enter a dose within the label.** For example, metformin 850 mg PO three times daily with meals (2,550 mg/day). Tell me if you want this and I'll enter it now.\n- **Route the high-dose order through pharmacy.** If a real protocol exists, the pharmacist or prescriber can enter it directly through your hospital's override or non-formulary process. That process should have its own verification and documentation.\n\nDo you want me to enter the 850 mg three-times-daily order, or would you rather go through pharmacy?"
      }
